{"id":"chatcmpl-39106f2c-2783-4838-8a29-60d658c99f63","object":"chat.completion","created":1795250653,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task required distinguishing between two laterality options for a radiological finding. The successful strategy combined a domain-expert query with a grounded localization tool, then resolved a discrepancy between tools by trusting the spatially-grounded output. The key insight is that laterality questions demand explicit spatial verification rather than relying on a single descriptive source.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When options differ only by laterality (left vs. right), explicitly query for spatial coordinates or image-position grounding rather than accepting a verbal description alone.\",\n    \"When two tools disagree (one reports 'none present' while another localizes findings), prefer the tool that returns grounded spatial evidence over the one returning free-text absence claims.\",\n    \"Translate radiological orientation carefully: image-right corresponds to patient-left, so verify the coordinate-to-anatomy mapping before committing to an answer.\",\n    \"Use a domain-expert tool first to narrow the question, then a grounding/localization tool to confirm the discriminating attribute (here, side).\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Ask for explicit laterality and coordinate grounding; cross-check verbal reports against spatial localization outputs.\",\n    \"Binary-choice discrimination\": \"Identify the single discriminating attribute between options (e.g., side, presence) and target tools specifically at that attribute.\",\n    \"Tool-disagreement resolution\": \"When tools conflict, weight grounded/structured evidence (coordinates, bounding regions) above free-text assertions of absence.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the discriminating attribute between options (laterality, presence, location) before selecting tools.\",\n    \"Verify coordinate-to-anatomy mapping (image-left vs. patient-left) before finalizing a laterality answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":467,"total_tokens":828,"completion_tokens":361,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":467},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":361}}}